          <change when="2025-02-26T10:22:13-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready.</change>
          <change when="2025-02-26T06:51:06-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Vote - Accept-Straight-to-Finalization - The reading Καισαριος is clear but should be printed Καίσαρ{ι}ος and credited as a PN correction. The editors already had Σεβασ&lt;τ&gt;οῦ, which can be left as is.</change>
          <change when="2025-01-01T10:00:22-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Gad">Submit - In line 5 I have made two changes. I can clearly see Καίσαριος in the digital image available. I can also see no tau in Σεβασοῦ. </change>
          <change when="2025-01-01T10:00:15-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Gad">Commit - In line 5 I have made two changes. I can clearly see Καίσαριος in the digital image available. I can also see no tau in Σεβασοῦ. </change>
          <change when="2025-01-01T09:58:06-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/Gad">Commit - In l.5 I can read clearly Καίσαριος and Σεβασοῦ, which are mistakes for Καίσαρος and Σεβαστοῦ respectively. The first mistake is commen cf. e.g. the the same mistake in l. 11 of this fragment https://papyri.info/ddbdp/p.louvre;3;177, which has been corrected fromt he schriber and noted by editor. As for Σεβασοῦ this could be regarded as an omision of the t after s, which is commen in papyri cf. e.g. Gignac I p. 66. If it were up to me I would have differentiated between the clear cases where one can see a t and where one cann´t..Here I can not clearly see the tau.  </change>
